From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:45:00 +0000
Subject: do not redefine libstdc++ _Atomic_word

When PARALLEL_ENABLED is not defined, Parallel.hh does
"typedef int _Atomic_word", but _Atomic_word is a reserved identifier
already defined by libstdc++ via <bits/atomic_word.h>, as "long" on
some architectures.  This causes a build failure on sparc64:

  Parallel.hh:70:13: error: conflicting declaration 'typedef int _Atomic_word'
  atomic_word.h:29:16: note: previous declaration as 'typedef long int _Atomic_word'

Only provide the fallback typedef when not using libstdc++.

Forwarded: no
---
 src/Parallel.hh | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Parallel.hh b/src/Parallel.hh
index b3d0eec..99e6bde 100644
--- a/src/Parallel.hh
+++ b/src/Parallel.hh
@@ -67,7 +67,13 @@
    //
    // parallel execution disabled, no need for atomicity
    //
+   // _Atomic_word is reserved and already defined by libstdc++, with
+   // an architecture-dependent type (e.g. long on sparc64), so only
+   // define it when not using libstdc++.
+   //
+# ifndef __GLIBCXX__
 typedef int _Atomic_word;
+# endif
 
 inline int atomic_fetch_add(volatile _Atomic_word & counter, int increment)
    { const int ret = counter;   counter += increment;   return ret; }
